1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:01:47,420
The prayer of part 4 continues here. Sometimes it rises in the mind of a lover of the Bhagavatam: what is the need of repeating these points so often? The praise has gone on long enough, tell the lila ahead. Why does Shukadeva Goswami bring this in again and again, and what is his purpose? We will hear it ahead. When Brahma offers praise he says this same thing. When the wives of the serpent offer praise they certainly say, You alone have made the world, You are the controller of the world. A living being does not quickly accept that everything belongs to the Lord. He may say it with the voice, but the feeling pressed into the heart from beginningless time, that I am this, this is mine, this thing is for me, I am its enjoyer, is very hard to know from the heart. So the Bhagavatam repeats it. By repetition, because the teaching is given more than once. [Brahma-sutra 4.1.1] The Brahma-sutra says that by constant repetition a thing takes effect upon the heart.

2
00:01:50,170 --> 00:03:24,760
This katha, which Nalakuvara and Manigriva are speaking, is not required for the Lord. The Lord is not the hearer. We are the hearers. This is being spoken for us. We have to understand that everything is Krishna's. His relation with these things is this close, and He is also beyond them. He is condensed eternity, knowledge, and bliss. This is the inert world. Between the Lord and this world there is a great difference. Still, the Lord is the cause of this universe. Without Him this universe has no existence. Everything is His. This universe is the Lord, and the Lord is also different from it. Nalakuvara and Manigriva are saying, O Krishna, O Krishna, O great yogi, You are the original person, beyond. The learned know that this universe, manifest and unmanifest, is Your form. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.29] Brahmana means one who is fixed in Brahman, and viduh means those who know. They know that this whole universe is Your form, and that it is not separate from You. Since the Lord is its mover, its maker, and also its material cause, this is His own energy.

3
00:03:24,760 --> 00:06:39,110
In the next verse they are saying that in the matter of this universe, in the matter of the living being, in the matter of every thing, You know completely, and You are also the controller of all. Both points are in one verse. You are the controller, and You know everything. In which second who thought what, who ate what, and through endless time ahead who will think what, when he will sneeze, when he will laugh, when he will sing, when he will weep, the Lord knows it all, of every single living being. This verse describes the Lord's abhijna, His being the knower. Yesterday a person was saying that one speaker of katha says, on the first verse of the Bhagavatam I can speak for a month. In it there is janmady asya yatah, and abhijnah. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 1.1.1] One quality of the Lord is described, abhijna. One who knows everything is called abhijna. Abhi means completeness, and jna means the knower. He knows everything. We cannot even imagine such a thing. To establish the Lord's knowing of all is one style of the Bhagavatam. We make a thing, and we also try to control it, but the limited things we have made go out of our control. Some article is stolen, and we do not even come to know. When a thing we made and kept is being stolen, we do not notice. In the most ordinary institution it cannot be noticed. In temples it is written here and there, be careful of your purse, and still it goes. There is no abhijna. It is carried in the pocket, and still it goes. What knower will we be of anything else? Ask someone, when you were in the womb, what were you thinking? He does not even remember whether he was there. How will the thinking be remembered? Which body is coming next, in which country, who the mother and father will be. The birth is already fixed. The Lord knows that.

4
00:06:40,520 --> 00:10:29,570
I know what is past, what is present, and what is yet to be, and no one knows Me. [Bhagavad-gita 7.26] He says, whatever has happened in the past, I know it all. I know the future. I know the present. You are the Lord of the body, the life-breath, the soul, the mind, and the senses of every embodied being. You are the controller. As I said, You made us act that low enjoyment, and through Narada's mouth You gave the curse. They are confirming that same point here. You alone are the controller of everyone's senses, of the life-airs, of the mind. You are the regulator. You are the Lord. Of all the beings in this universe, from an insect up to Brahma, each has a body. If there is a disease in the body, in the life-air, or in a sense, one should bow to the Lord: please set it right, because You alone are the controller, You alone are the regulator. It is under Him. How long He will give us the power to see. I accept that I am the controller, but along with me there are many demigods who live on the senses and live in the mind. They too are regulators. Then Nalakuvara and Manigriva say, tvam ekah. Only You, and no one else. When no demigod is the regulator, how can a human being be the regulator? There is a body, so a man says to everyone, this body is mine, this is my child, this is my wife. In the body there are senses, and there is a mind. The meaning of that saying is, all this is mine, I control it. In this the Lord, bound to the mortar, had as it were said, I do not control, time controls. Then they say, tvam eva kalo bhagavan. You Yourself are time. Time is not something else. Time is the name of Your own power of will. We accept that time is the maker of this world, its maintainer, and its destroyer. But You Yourself are time.

5
00:10:32,560 --> 00:13:17,150
So Lord Sri Krishna, who is a child, it does not feel right to call Him the Lord, because what is seen here is a child. Still they are saying, You Yourself are time, fully able. You Yourself are Vishnu. You Yourself are the imperishable Lord. You are Vishnu, and You Yourself are time. In truth, the Vishnu-hood of Vishnu is You. You Yourself are everything. And You are avyaya, without decay. In Your memory, in Your knowledge, in Your rule, in Your position, there is never any spending away. Avyaya, indestructible. In this world, every post other than the Lord's, of the demigods and of human beings, is always being spent. Today there is strength in the body. Tomorrow it must be spent. The intellect is spent. The power of sight is spent. The power to walk does not remain in the legs. Everything is spent. Even after becoming old, and even while seized by many diseases, a man says, I am Shiva. Outside, Shiva has no power to walk, and they have become Shiva, I am Brahman. I am Brahman. Brahman he is. In this condition he should serve the Supreme Brahman. The soul of the living being is beyond the body. He is Brahman, and he is the servant of the Supreme Brahman. For how many people, in a pamphlet, here and there, their disciples or other people keep writing, our guru is directly the Lord, this person is the Lord. But the Lord is in the hospital. That too is heard, outside. The Lord is performing the pastime of being admitted to that hospital. So the word ekah, the One, is being used here.

6
00:13:18,720 --> 00:16:51,150
That ekah is above, and in the later word there is eva. Eva also speaks of the same One. Today he is an emperor, he has become a king, and tomorrow the name and the mark are gone. Of the Lord it cannot be said, from when He will be. He simply is. Even 'is' cannot be applied, because 'is' is applied to a thing whose past and future are fixed as something. So scripture says that both asti and nasti cannot be applied to the Lord. Asti names a material thing that has existence, and nasti means what is not there at all. This point comes in the Hamsa-guhya prayers of the Sixth Canto. All these are material dealings. When we say, from when the Lord will be, that sentence is wrong. We can say beginningless. From beginningless time the Lord is as He is. He is that beautiful, that knowing, the opulence is that much, everything is there. No decay is ever going to happen, and nothing is going to go away from Him. Like the sun. Take it for some time. From when the sun is, its heat has been the brightness of life. A few years ago it came in some newspaper that the sun's heat is going to decrease, something should be replaced, it should be considered how we will give heat to the world in place of the sun. That is the thinking of fools. And two or four years after that, here and there the heat broke a record. The sun's heat is never going to leave. Unlimited splendor. It is said in the Brahma-samhita. Rather, at the end of creation the sun's power is increased a hundredfold. They give a hundredfold heat, to burn this world, and Lord Sankarshana. In a power that decreases, this unlimited splendor is not there. The sun-god is a lord. The universe, or Krishna, from beginningless time is joined with endless opulence. As He is, so He is. This word avyaya is very important. Whatever is His, all of it is without decay.

7
00:16:54,060 --> 00:20:13,350
And when this is said, the Lord as it were reasons. You people are saying that We Ourselves are the form of the world, We are the controller, this and that. Then how are We the form of the world? We have heard that nature is the cause. Then they say, You are the mahat, You are subtle nature, made of passion, goodness, and ignorance. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.31] You Yourself are the great, the mahat-tattva. You Yourself are nature, and in the subtle state, as pradhana, You Yourself are that too. The nature whose three qualities are passion, goodness, and ignorance is You. That means it is Your energy. They are speaking with the intention that energy and the possessor of energy are non-different. You Yourself are subtle nature. You Yourself are the mahat-tattva. In passion, ignorance, and goodness, You Yourself are there. You Yourself are the person, the adhyaksha. You Yourself are the person. You Yourself are nature, and You Yourself are the person. You Yourself are the person, the indweller of all, and You Yourself are the presiding witness. Adhyaksha means the witness of all. Witness has this same meaning. The word aksha is the eye. From aksha comes akshi, the one with eyes. A witness means one with eyes. One who has eyes is called a witness. And adhyaksha has this same meaning: one whose eye is everywhere, who holds knowledge of all by right. While controlling, while holding authority, he is called the president. The meaning of president is not that he is only glancing in pieces and has no power. The meaning is that wherever his sight goes, he is also the controller of that. By authority his eyes are there, the information is there, and the power of control is there. Then he is called adhyaksha. You know everything, and along with that You are the presiding witness.

8
00:20:13,740 --> 00:25:30,440
And the knower of the changes of every field. The knower of whatever change is in all the fields. The Lord has said the meaning of kshetra in the Gita. All material things are called the field. The whole of nature is the field. Earth is the field. Air, water, fire, all are the field. The bodies made by the joining of all these, of water, of land, of the sky, are also fields. And the mind, intelligence, and ego placed in those fields are also fields. In the field there are two kinds of change. One is the subtle field. What thoughts are rising in the intelligence and in the ego, what wave is rising, grief, bewilderment, joy, dejection. He is the knower of all of those. And in this gross body, childhood, youth, old age, disease, a boil, a pimple, a cold, a cough, hunger, thirst, whatever change is happening, the body thinning from old age, growing, He has knowledge of all of it. There is knowledge of the gross body, and there is knowledge of the whole subtle body. The knower of the changes of every field. Here I will not explain the words kshetra and kshetrajna, because all of you have been reading Bhagavad-gita for a long time. It should be understood in the form of a sutra. I am the knower of all the fields. The Lord is the knower of all. [Bhagavad-gita, chapter 13] On this the Lord again, as it were, asked a question. If I am the material cause of the world, then when there is knowledge of some thing, that it is this long, this wide, that it is green, yellow, red, since I Myself am the form of the thing and I Myself am the material cause, knowledge of a thing should be counted as knowledge of Me. But it does not happen so. Scientists have knowledge of the world. What the material changes are. Here the word guna means the mind, the intelligence, the ego, the eye, the ear, the nose, the senses. In the Sanskrit used in scripture, guna sometimes names a sense and sometimes a change. These are the qualities of nature, the changes. As this book is in front of us. The book is green. Our eye is taking it. But this book cannot have knowledge of our eye. If someone asks the book, do you have knowledge of the eye of the one who is reading? If I close my eye, the book does not see our eye. Our eye is seeing it. In the same way the Lord is the seer of things. He is not the thing seen. By material eyes, by material intelligence, the Lord is not grasped. A material thing is one thing. A non-material thing is another. The Lord is non-material. He is the controller of material things, their mover. Let no material thing, having grasped something, think, I have caught the Lord. Speech and the senses cannot catch the Lord, cannot understand Him. The soul is conscious, spiritual. The soul can receive the Lord.

9
00:25:32,330 --> 00:31:09,840
On this, as if the Lord had said, then a living being can know Me. Then Nalakuvara and Manigriva say, who in this world, covered by the modes, is able to know You, who are established before the creation? [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.32] Every living being in this world is covered by the modes, covered by the body. By the mind, the intelligence, the ego, the things given by nature, the living being's knowledge is covered. How can a person covered like that know You? You are prak-siddha, already established. The meaning is not only that the Lord is before our birth. From birth, of course He is before. But in nature there was no thing at all. There was no sky, no air, no fire, nothing. Before that, the Lord is. That is called established before. Before nature, that is, before the work of creating this world made by nature, the Lord is. Later everyone's birth happened, things were made. And on top of that the living being is covered by the modes, stuck in material things. In the body he has made the intelligence of I. He has been given a material intelligence and a material mind. All of it is a covering, the covering of the modes. How can such a person know You? There is the covering of nature, and the Lord is from long before, made of consciousness. He cannot know. At the very first, when Brahma appeared, when Brahma took birth, even Brahma did not know the Lord. In his mind there was an inquiry, where has the lotus flower taken birth from? There is some cause of it. Someone has given me birth. But who they are, Brahma did not know. By his own intelligence, by his own effort, he undertook a search. He entered the lotus stem and went down. Think, where the lotus has grown from, that will be our cause. He could not reach the Lord's navel. Going down the lotus stem took the years of many kalpas. The stem of the lotus is that long. One boy said, his breath must have given out, that is why he came running back. Whatever it was, Brahma did not reach the Lord's navel. He became hopeless. Having become hopeless, he came and sat again on the lotus flower. Sitting there he was meditating on the Lord, on his own cause. At that same time two words were heard, tapa, tapa. Practice austerity, practice austerity. Then his whole knowledge was given. When this is the condition of Brahma in this world, that knowledge of his own cause, the Lord, is not his by himself, how will another person, created by Brahma, know? When Brahma's sons took birth, all were inquiring about the Lord. But by taking shelter of Brahma they all became knowers, like Narada. Brahma taught all of them. Then Narada distributes knowledge. In this way, by the line. How will anyone know by himself? Who is there who is able to know You? How can a living being dependent on the modes know?

10
00:31:13,320 --> 00:33:42,040
Unto You, the Lord, Vasudeva, the creator, whose glory is covered by the qualities that shine from Yourself, unto Brahman, we bow. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.33] You are unknowable like this. So we cannot dare to know You. We can only bow to You. So we are bowing to You. To such an unknowable Supersoul, to Brahman, we are bowing. O You who are full of opulence, we are bowing to You. And You have also been the son of Vasudeva, we bow to You. O creator, maker and mover of the world, we bow to You. Then the Lord was as if astonished. He says, why are we giving some false faith? Where am I Brahman, the Supersoul, this, the creator? Then they say, whose glory is covered by the qualities shining from Himself. The word guna has come with two meanings. By these qualities You have hidden Your opulence, covered it. In truth You are Brahman. There is no other shore of You. Who is there who can tie a rope at Your waist? But You Yourself have covered Your own opulence. You are Vasudeva. By this verse, Nalakuvara and Manigriva actually want to remind the Lord, for the work of the demigods. In their mind there is this point, that we are demigods, and for doing the work of the demigods the Lord has taken an avatara in Mathura. One acharya comments. He says, they are reminding Him, do not only drag the mortar like this. Go to Mathura and kill the demons as well. The poor demigods are greatly unhappy. Obeisances unto Vasudeva.

11
00:33:46,130 --> 00:38:41,690
The Lord says, when I am unknowable in this way, and no one can know Me, then how did you come to know? How did the knowledge come to you that I am the Lord, that I am the Supreme? Then they say, not only to us, the knowledge will come to anyone that You are the Lord. When You manifest Your own body among those who bear bodies. You are without a material body. You are free of a material body. Still You manifest Your form of condensed consciousness in this world. When You take an avatara, when You manifest Your conscious form in the world, whatever the shape may be, like Vamana, or Lord Nrishimha, or You Yourself as a child. Then, whose avataras are recognized. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.34] By which the avatara becomes known. It becomes known that it is You. How does it become known? By the powers. By Your acts of valor, by Your uncommon lilas, it becomes known that this is the Lord. You perform acts of valor that have no comparison anywhere. No one is able to do the like of them. Whenever You take an avatara and perform the lila of the Lord, another living being cannot do it. It is certain that only You can do it. Valor without an equal, and valor beyond all. Atishaya means surpassing all, and atulya means what has no equal, the most uncommon lila. As when You accepted the Varaha avatara, You lifted the whole earth on the tip of Your teeth and came along easily, laughing. Did Brahma not come to know, and Marichi and the sages, that this is the Lord? Brahma had sneezed. He had fallen into worry. And from the sneeze Lord Varaha was born. But in a moment He grew so much, He began to roar like a vast mountain, He dove into the ocean. Brahma understood at once that this is the Lord. So, whose avataras are recognized. Your avatara becomes known. He performs valor and lila uncommon among all who bear bodies. Having searched out the earth, having lifted the earth, He brought it on the tip of the teeth. The earth rests on the tip of Your tusk, like a dark spot resting on the moon. O Keshava, who have taken the form of the boar, glory, O Lord of the universe. [Jayadeva, Dashavatara] So, on Your great white teeth this earth appears like a dark spot. The whole earth was nothing before the teeth of Lord Varaha. First those great teeth, and an earth many times larger than the teeth. No bearer of a body can be like that. He cannot perform such valor. And just now, You are a child, but You pulled the rope tied at Your waist, and these two trees were uprooted from the root. While thousands of the kings of elephants, even together, could not uproot them. Does it not become known that You are the Lord? Will any child do this? Will any child uproot such a tree? He cannot uproot even a small plant. Will he uproot trees this heavy? So it becomes known.

12
00:38:43,770 --> 00:44:12,070
One who bears a body is fighting hunger, fighting thirst, fighting sleep. What work will he do above that? Very great people have been, but the list of their works remained limited. Whatever the Lord does, He does without end. When the need came, He held Mandarachala. Lifting a mountain is the Lord's habit. Here in this Braj He lifted Govardhana. But the lila the Lord performs in Braj has one astonishing uncommonness. Our acharyas have said, He does everything by His own sweet form. On Mandarachala the churning was going on, at great speed. Of that Mandarachala mountain it is said that in its base there were very vast rocks, golden like mung. There was a great bulge and roughness. And a mountain like that was being rubbed on the Lord's back. The rubbing was on the Lord's back. When the milk was being churned, such great waves were rising in it, whirlpools were forming, from which the great tortoises and the timingila fish fled far away. But how did the Lord experience the rubbing of that vast mountain? Again and again it is said in the Bhagavatam, it seemed as if someone were scratching the Lord's back, and a happy sleep came to the Lord, and He slept. The Bhagavatam describes it so. Such a vast mountain is being rubbed, and rocks like mung are striking, khar-khar on the back, and a very happy sleep is coming. One acharya speaks this mood. Lord Kurma is sleeping, and by the air of His breath as He sleeps the ocean is moved. So they say, may the air of the Lord's breath protect us. A prayer in this way. All this is unfit for those who bear bodies. If anyone ordinary could do it, then one might say, he has become the Lord. As it would be known, a dam is to be built, and one man lifts several mountains, brings them, and builds the dam. Then it will be known that he is the Lord. As the Lord built the bridge. The stones floated. Is there an engineer at this time who touches a stone with his hand and it simply floats? There is no one. There was no pillar in it. And do you know how wide that road was? They tell that it was ten yojanas wide. One yojana is called four kos. And it was a hundred yojanas long. The bridge was eight hundred miles long. So great a bridge was built, to cross the ocean. There was no one bringing a crane. Nothing. They brought stones, the monkeys lifting and lifting. And on one, the name of Rama was written. They floated, but they drifted here and there. When the name of Rama was written, they became steady like a packed load. By the Lord's glory the stone floated. By the glory of Sri Raghuvira the stone became a boat. They are doing the work of wood, and they began to carry others across. This is called the Lord. Among those who bear bodies it becomes known that this person is the Lord, by what is in His valor, in His act, which does not fit the other bearers of bodies.

13
00:44:12,200 --> 00:47:49,200
And it fits such a Lord. You have appeared at this time for the birth of all the worlds and for their vibhava. You are the same Lord, for the coming to be of every world and for its liberation. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.35] You are that same Lord, that same Supreme Brahman, the Supersoul. You, for the rising of all the worlds, for their growth, and for vibhava. Vibhava means the going of worldly becoming, that by which becoming leaves, for liberation. To free everyone. That is, by manifesting Your own lila, to show the path of liberation, to have devotion done, You have taken an avatara at this time. Now. In truth You are the master of all things, the giver of all enjoyment, of dharma, artha, kama, and moksha. The husband of all blessings. Sri Krishna is the husband of all blessings, the giver to all. In this world, whoever needs money, the Lord can give it to him, and He can give so much that no one else can give that much. Until today there have been many devotees of Shiva in this world, and of Brahma, like Hiranyakashipu. There have been many devotees of Durga, like Kamsa. There have been devotees of the Lord, and the Lord gave them wealth, like Dhruva Maharaj. The wealth given to Dhruva Maharaj, Ravana and the others do not have even a croreth part of it. They cannot even imagine it. Dhruva Maharaj has received Dhruvaloka. That is Vaikuntha. It is not destroyed in the dissolution. So limitless is what the Lord gives. This He has given even more to His own devotees. Other people cannot give it, because of all things, of dharma, of liberation, of enjoyments, You are the Lord of all. Descended by the portion of the parts. By His own parts, by His own portion. Portion also means fortune. By the fortune of His own parts, the living beings, You have appeared at this time. Such is the fortune of the living beings that You have appeared now. We are recognizing it. If there is any longing in anyone's mind, any wish, he should say it to the Lord. In truth the giver of all things is Krishna. It is their mistake that people keep asking from someone else. No one can fulfill a wish. No goddess, no demigod, and no human being can fulfill a wish. The Lord fulfills the wish of the living being. So He is the husband of blessings. Therefore they are bowing to Him.

14
00:47:49,200 --> 00:53:21,830
Obeisances, O supreme welfare. Obeisances, O supreme good. Unto Vasudeva, the peaceful, the Lord of the Yadus, obeisances. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.36] O supreme welfare, we offer You our obeisances. O supreme good, we offer You our obeisances. From the Lord, the welfare of the living beings does come. In truth, welfare is the Lord Himself. The Lord alone is welfare. Welfare means happiness. O form of condensed happiness, O happiness itself, we are bowing to You. So You Yourself are happiness. Why will happiness be searched for apart from the Lord? If the Lord is attained, the greatest joy, the supreme joy, will be attained. This is for the devotees without material desire, that You Yourself are the supreme welfare. They want the Lord's love. But in this life also something is needed, to eat and drink in happiness, to live, a house and a door. So they say, obeisances, O supreme mangala. The Lord Himself is the supreme mangala. Mangala means both the destination and the path of the journey. Life is crossed in happiness, by Your mercy. In truth, someone may say, we are desireless devotees, but in this life a great need comes, for every life. Of eating, and along with that, that this intelligence also remain upon our own people, that they stay joined to dharma and to the Lord. In this way let them live happily, and having lived, at the end go to the Lord's abode. This is called mangala. The word mangala is used in the sense of the destination. Obeisances to the supreme mangala means, O Lord, by Your mercy the living being stays happy in this world, in this life also, there is no anxiety, and at the end he attains Your lotus feet. O supreme welfare, obeisances to You. O supreme good, obeisances to You. If mangala is wanted, Krishna's worship should be done. If welfare is wanted, and the highest happiness, then Krishna's worship should be done. Unto Vasudeva, and unto the peaceful, unto the Lord of the Yadus, obeisances. O son of Vasudeva, obeisances to You. And the mischief You were doing, so much of it, at this time peace has come. You have become peaceful, upon being bound. Here this is the meaning of shanta. Peace has come. The speech has stopped. You are completely silent. I wanted to hear. Obeisances unto the Lord of the Yadus. O protector of the Yadus, obeisances to You. The Yadus have all become demigods. Demigods themselves have taken birth in the form of the Yadus. So they are indicating, keep doing the child's lila in Braj like this, and also remove the burden of the earth. You will now remove the unhappiness of the demigods. They are calling Him the protector of the Yadus. Or the people of the Vrishni family are also Yadus. So they are saying, O son of Vasudeva, O peaceful one, and O protector of the Yadus, obeisances to You. The word shantaya is very full, and a second meaning is also being given. In itself, the form of Lord Vishnu is that He is free of attachment and hatred, He is peaceful. The Lord is in truth greatly beautiful. He is not sharp, He is not a trouble, He is peaceful. And the other demigods are fierce. But here He is in truth peaceful. They are only offering praise without anger, bowing again and again, touching the feet. When people say namah they say it while touching the feet. And the Lord was sitting peaceful and silent. So He is peaceful, the Lord of the Yadus.

15
00:53:24,930 --> 00:57:44,530
The demigods could not have stayed. And if these two stayed, the Lord could not have done the lila ahead. Then, for a short while, by the Lord's inconceivable energy, Mother Yashoda became absorbed in work over there. She did not come to know at all that two demigods had appeared, and that after worshiping Krishna they had gone to heaven. Nothing was known. The people call Him Shyama. Please permit us, O complete one. We are the servants of Your servants. Our sight of the Lord came by the sage's mercy. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.37] O Bhuman, O You who are complete in every way. They are remembering the time when they were not bound by the rope. Now He has been bound by the rope. So this is Your astonishing lila. O complete one, You are complete in every way. But please give us an order. Please give us permission. We are the servants of Your servants. We have done no quality of our own. We are the servants of Your servants. So please order us, what service of Yours we should do. And what felt so to me, that the Lord is silent, they experienced along with it that the Lord is saying, move quickly from here, there is more lila to do. There is no speaking. It is like a very heavy speech. In truth, if you keep speaking to someone, and the person is sitting grave and silent, the mind will feel, he does not like our presence. So they say, anujanihi. The meaning of anujanihi is, then please give the order. Now give us the order to go. But before going they want to speak with the Lord. This much has been understood, that the Lord wants them to go. It was very well done that through Narada You made our opulence fall. We received the body of a tree, we received Your favor, we received Your company. When the Lord was speaking nothing at all, these people decided that You also want them to go. So whatever the Lord's order is, whatever the wish is, that should be followed. So we will go to that same place from which we were made trees. Then we are going to Alakapuri. This is Your wish, we understand. You gave so beautiful a body, You gave a freed body, You delivered us, and this is Your hope, that we go to that same place, Alakapuri.

16
00:57:45,140 --> 01:00:55,930
More establishment. Let our tongue describe Your qualities. May our speech be in the telling of Your qualities, our two ears in the katha, our two hands in Your work, our mind in the remembrance of Your feet, our head in bowing to the world that is Your home, and our sight in seeing the saints, who are Your own bodies. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.38] Let them describe Your qualities a little more. Let our speech remain in the speaking of the qualities. Let both our ears stay joined to the katha. Saying both ears means that our hearing remain completely in Your katha, and hear no other talk. It is not said in the singular. It is said shravanau, in the dual. On this Sanatana Goswami says, let the whole function of the ears be joined only to hearing the katha. And let both our hands remain in Your service, in Your work. And let the mind remain in the remembrance of Your lotus feet, in the remembrance of Your beautiful form, in the qualities. And the head in bowing to You. Let our head stay engaged in offering You obeisances. How You are. The home is the world. The world itself is Your home, and there the work of the world is. Braj is Your home. So let our head stay engaged in bowing to such a Braj. Then let them bow to You together with Your home, with Braj. In the dust of Braj. And our sight, the power of our eye, let it stay joined to seeing Your devotees, who are counted as Your body. In truth the Lord lives in the hearts of the devotees. So the devotees, the sadhus, are called Krishna's body. They are Krishna's body. Krishna dwells in their heart. Govinda is always present in your heart. Your own bodies. Or the forms of Yours that are established in the temple, let us always see those forms. Let our sight stay joined to seeing. This is a very important point. Sometimes the question rises, why did Nalakuvara and Manigriva go from Braj to Alakapuri. They themselves should have stayed here. But in truth the Lord wants the preaching of the Lord's lilas, of the truths of the Lord, in the whole world, in the society of the demigods, in the society of the demons, in the society of human beings. Nalakuvara and Manigriva will go to heaven and tell this lila. Then there will be knowledge of the Lord's glory. People will be joined to Krishna. Then their unhappiness will end.

17
01:00:58,710 --> 01:06:54,900
Here their feeling is being told in the Bhakti-rasayana in this way. When Nalakuvara and Manigriva became ready to go to heaven, they say to the Lord, O Lord, we are asking something at Your feet. Although from the outside You are a helpless master, bound, You are the complete person. Our father is the king of kings. That means we are going to our father. He is the king even of kings. There is no lack of wealth. The nine treasures stay in our command. The daughters of the yakshas are beautiful. So we do not ask a beautiful woman from You. We do not desire a beautiful woman. It is not that we do not desire because they are already there. In truth there is no wish in their mind, not for wealth, not for fame, not for people, not for a beautiful woman. Asking for that is useless for us, because all of it is already easy to obtain. Father is Kuvera. There are the nine treasures. And the beautiful women of the yakshas are for us. You have given a form such that Kamadeva himself will desire our form. You have also given a body fully young. And as far as the question of a vehicle, there is Pushpaka itself. So, nothing else is to be prayed for. This is what they are asking, that we may not forget Your name Krishna. Let Your name always be remembered, and let us always sing the qualities, let us always do Your devotion, wherever we stay. Please give us this mercy, and nothing else is wanted. And everything else is with us. This is a style of speaking, that everything else is with us, only give this one thing, that the name of Krishna not be forgotten. See further in this boon. First of all, speech in the telling of the qualities. Why are they asking this boon first, that my speech remain in the description of Your qualities? Sridhara Swami says, I am not reading it after reading the whole Sanskrit, I am telling the mood. Nalakuvara and Manigriva, let our speech stay joined to the description of Your qualities. Guna means mercy, fame, and further opulence. But they are saying guna by making it the body of the prayer. The rule is that the thing by which a person's work was accomplished, he gives that the first place. The first place in this is the description of the qualities. They are asking first, let the tongue stay joined to describing the qualities, because by the quality, by the speech, their deliverance had happened. And the Lord is sending them to a place where the intoxication of wealth can come again. There is again the fear of the intoxication of wealth. So they say, let our eyes always stay joined to the sight of the saints. As before our sight was joined to the sight of women, let it not be joined now. Let the sight be in seeing the saints. Let the sight be joined to the sight of saints, of devotees, of sadhus. In this world everyone's sight stays naturally joined to the sight of women. Keeping a photograph in the house. Nowadays there is also the salon shop, and in it the pictures of actresses are hung. The hair is being cut, in the salon, and the sight is joined to a sight of that kind. In this way life will go useless. So let our sight stay joined to the sight of sadhus. Lord, give the boon. They are in the heart as the Supersoul. Let it be so that the sight always stays joined to the sight of sadhus, who are counted as Your body.

18
01:06:58,010 --> 01:11:49,870
This depends on Your wish. We have no need of our own. You have many devotees, and many pray to You. Whatever is Your taste, or according to their taste, give whatever is to be given. But let the sight stay joined to the sight of sadhus. The meaning is that the Lord will give the company of sadhus, and then the sight will happen. For a long time they had the sight of women, they had these sights. So in what a bad destination they remained. And one day there was only the sight of a sadhu, of Narada. That was all. It feels good to explain this verse for a long time, but the time is completely finished, so I do not want to read further. The Lord was smiling. He was smiling at this, that the bound living beings offer My praise, they pray. I give liberation. What can I not do. So the Lord was smiling. He was not smiling as a child's lila. And having smiled, He spoke. The Lord said. The supremely beautiful Lord is speaking. Here Shukadeva Swami is using the words the beautiful Lord. So the meaning is, the beautiful Lord is speaking. The Lord bound in the mortar is speaking. He says, this was known to Me from before, what the merciful sage did. By his words, the fall of those blinded by the intoxication of wealth was a favor. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.40] He is not speaking a lisping speech, and He is not speaking a voice deep as a cloud. He is speaking clearly. From before, He knew all this. Known to Me, even before, this. From before it was known that Narada had given you people a curse. It was not a curse in truth. It was Narada's mercy. This was known to Me. When those blinded by wealth, by words, the fall, the favor. Mercy. That was the sadhu's boon. Such a thing was known to Me from before. From when? From before it was known. It is only three years since the birth, and in between who had told Him that it was known from before? This itself is the Lord's being the Lord. And if someone asks Me, asks the Lord, had these also taken birth before? What had not been heard upon you people was his mercy. Of the sadhus who see equally, and still more of those whose selves are made for Me, by their sight a person's bondage does not remain, as the eye's bondage does not remain before the sun. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.41] My sadhus are equal-sighted. They are My devotees. When they are not seen, darkness settles. Then the eyes are in a way closed, they cannot see. As soon as this sun rises, it seems the eyes have opened and sight begins. So when one sees My devotees, bondage does not remain. Ignorance does not remain. He is telling with attention that when a person in this way sees My devotee, a sadhu, and remembers, then ignorance cannot remain in his life, and the bondage of work cannot remain. As when the sun rises the bondage of the eyes does not remain, and the power of seeing comes.

19
01:11:54,390 --> 01:16:53,770
You two, go to your own home. To the house. Now you have become My devotees. Love for you has arisen in Me. The supreme love you desired has been born in Me, from which there is no return to worldly becoming. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.10.42] Now go, you two for whom I am the supreme, Nalakuvara, to your home. The supreme feeling for both of you has already arisen in Me. In Me, meaning He is saying it while showing His own form. I who am bound to the mortar, He is saying it while showing the feeling, that your supreme feeling for Me has happened. The children are understanding that He is saying, you people love Us. That is natural. They are understanding it as natural. The supreme feeling has happened. What kind of feeling? Abhava. On the coming of which feeling, worldly becoming does not happen again. The living being does not fall again into birth and death. Such supreme love of you both has happened in Me, which you were desiring, the desired one. From a long time, from the very sight of Narada until now, the love you people were desiring, were wanting, that supreme love has been attained by you. By My mercy, or by Narada's mercy. You people may go. In some matter, they did not want to go. But when the Lord said that the supreme goal of a person, which is love at My feet, has been born in you people, fully born, you may go. It is no matter. The Lord is sending them to preach His own devotion. Hearing this much, they began to offer obeisances. So they are also bowing to the mortar, and also bowing to the rope. Obeisances unto the rope, the abode of shining splendor. [Damodarashtakam] Unto the rope, obeisances to that rope in which Krishna is bound. Shukadeva Goswami says that when they circumambulated the Lord in this way, and offered obeisances, again and again, they offered obeisances again and again. They would walk after bowing, then circumambulate and bow, then bow again. Unto the mortar to which He was bound. They were bowing to the mortar, to the Lord who was bound in the mortar. They were bowing to Him again and again, that You have delivered us. They were bowing to the rope. They were bowing to the Lord. And they were bowing to the children sitting there. There was no satiation in bowing. Having bowed, then they went. They set out toward the northern direction. They did not go by the sky. Through the whole day, and walking and walking in Braj, going that way, outside the village, then they went like an airplane, by the path of the sky. But in the beginning, on the ground itself, toward the north. Om namo bhagavate vasudevaya. Leaving the one bound to the mortar, Nalakuvara and Manigriva went.

20
01:16:55,500 --> 01:21:00,520
They understood that the Lord likes to be bound to the mortar. It is pleasing to Him. And being bound in the rope is pleasing not only to the Lord. It is also pleasing to His devotees that He remain bound to the mortar. So we are not telling the lila of His being untied just now. He will be untied this very day, but we will say it in the common way. When Krishna was bound to the mortar, what condition of His was happening at that time. Mother Yashoda had gone and driven everyone away, do not make a crowd here, go. You people yourselves have spoiled our boy. When a person is in anger, he lays the blame on anyone. So the gopis went away. But it was told to the children. Mother Yashoda has kept Him bound since morning. The moment he heard this much, Sri Balarama came running. He has been kept bound. Sri Balarama has the feeling of a parent's love for Lord Krishna, because he is the guru, he is the elder brother. For doing this very affection. And He is the supreme person, the Lord Himself. He has been bound in this way, so a very great offense is happening. And I see, I go. But the gopi had said that Yashoda has bound Him. Still Sri Balarama came. Before that is the lila. How Krishna is weeping. Bound, He is sobbing. From time to time He would begin to sob. Tears would well up. In one song Srila Surdas has sung, the young boy fills His eyes with water again and again. Kumara means Krishna. The young boy, in the eye, in the locana, fills tears again and again. From time to time He begins to sob. Why is He weeping? Not from this punishment. Again and again He is remembering, the mother who loved me so much, what has happened to her today? So remembering the mother's former affection, and remembering today's hard behavior, again and again there is regret, and He is weeping. The young boy fills His eyes with water again and again. Krishna weeps again and again, He sobs, and tears well up in the eyes. The child's face. Yashoda of the heart, look a little. Ah, some gopi will say, look, Yashoda, look once at your son's face. What a condition the poor child's is. Look once.

21
01:21:01,610 --> 01:25:13,510
Untie from the belly the rope that cannot be borne, and put down the hard stick in the hand. The young boy fills His eyes with water again and again. Untie, from the belly, the rope that cannot be borne. This rope you are tying, you have tied, untie it, untie it. And put the stick down from the hand. Otherwise something will happen to your son. Some illness will happen. He has become so afraid, He is weeping so much. One, untie the rope, and put the stick down. The yogurt was washed, why are you doing this? It is not known how so much hardness has come into your heart. Upon a baby, darkness. Upon one baby, upon a child, so much cruelty is happening, so much darkness is happening in you also. Tears are spread on the face. Drops of tears. And the poor child had eaten butter, what the monkeys had snatched and looted, so He had eaten it too. The Lord has not been able to wipe the face. Butter is also smeared, in one or two places, on the mouth. And there are drops of tears. The face, tears, and a particle of butter. Look with the eye at the beauty. The young boy fills His eyes with water again and again. The particle of butter that is there, smeared on the face, wherever it is smeared. Surdas says it, in the feeling of that gopi, that it is looking like the moon. And the small particles of tears are glittering like stars. And the whole dark face of Shyama is looking like the blue sky. They have not been able to wipe. They are not able to wipe the butter, and not the tears either. The face, tears, and a particle of butter. Look with the eye at the beauty. As if a flowing ocean of nectar, pearls, and the stars of the night. Shyama. He fills the eyes again and again. I do not know by which piety He appeared, in which home of Nanda of Braj. It is not known, Yashoda, by the glory of which piety such a good boy took birth in your house. Ah, upon Him, body, mind, and wealth, everything should be offered. A little yogurt was wasted, butter was wasted, a pot was broken. What has happened from this? However much loss has happened, take a hundred times from our house, but untie Him. Mother Yashoda says, you, you will take a pot from your house, you will take butter, but if His habit is being spoiled, how will that be made right? You are showing wealth. Coming every day, you were letting Him be tempted. Today mercy is coming. Mother Yashoda speaks in this way.

22
01:25:14,100 --> 01:31:25,790
Then some gopi told Balarama that your brother has been bound today. The cowherd woman told that He is bound. Since early morning your younger brother, Yashoda has fixed Him bound to the mortar. Yashoda has bound Him, and that too bound against the mortar. This is how one is bound in a house, kept bound somewhere on one's own bed. So He has been bound against the mortar. It was heard in this way. So Sri Balarama came. How Sri Balarama is coming, and on seeing Krishna what condition of his also happens, that is the description. Hearing this, Haladhara came. Haladhara came, having heard. Shyama is bound to the mortar, and at once both eyes filled. So Sri Balarama also began to weep. Seeing Krishna bound, tears filled Balarama's eyes. Krishna was already weeping. These two Lords are weeping. Today He has reached a poor condition. Seeing it, he began to weep. Weeping, he says, how many times I told you, Kanhaiya, and well done, both hands are tied. I forbade you many times. Do not steal in this way. Do not do mischief in this way. So you are having a fine enjoyment. The hand has been closed. Well done, both hands are closed today. Today both hands have been closed. I forbade you again and again. He is saying it while weeping. Will you still leave this crookedness? He has come to Mother with both hands joined. From today you will leave mischief of this kind. You will not steal now. So he is asking while making Mother hear. Let Krishna say it, with hands joined. He will go and say, now He is saying that now He will not do it. You will not steal now. You will not do mischievous work now. Krishna is weeping, He is speaking nothing. So Sri Balarama came to Mother, to Yashoda. Rather untie Him and bind me. On leaving the house I did not meet a good omen. Today as I was going from the house the omen did not happen, it was not good. If I had stayed here I would not have let Krishna be bound in this way. Today I did not leave the house after seeing the face of a good man. So Mother, leave Shyama and bind me. If you have the wish to bind, then leave Him, Krishna, and bind me. My life, my living, my wealth, is Kanhaiya. Do not bind His arms. Krishna is my life, He is my living. And His arm. Bind me. Balarama's meaning in saying it was, untie Him. This was the meaning. If he says it like this, she will untie. And when she did not agree to untie, and said, you go, you do your own work. Then Balarama says, you know who I am. Having said this much, toward his own form. Then Balarama began to weep again. From Mother's scolding he began to weep. And going, with his blue cloth, with his blue garment, he began to wipe the Lord's tears. He was not very much bigger than Krishna. They were almost the same. So he is wiping the tears. The Lord is sobbing. And when Balarama said to Mother, untie Him, and Mother said, I will never untie, and you also go, then Sri Krishna began to weep still harder. There had been one hope, that the brother will come and untie. That also went, hopelessness. He began to weep. So the tears welled up. And then Balarama began to wipe the tears. And having wiped the tears, he says again to Mother Yashoda, the second time, with compassion. Now the heat that was there, he had wanted to show his own form, that stopped, and he began to pray. Why, Yashoda Maiya, have you bound the child Kanhaiya? Why, Yashoda Maiya? This sitting stops on this song.
